From 7366e259dcc45e5f1de61749cabdf31b2c35e0a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vishwajitvm <vishwajitmall50@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 11:55:14 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(console): the CLI is @strutvane/framework; doctor fails
 on a second kernel (B6)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The CLI still called itself @strutvane/cli. Its doctor told apps to
`pnpm add -D @strutvane/cli`, which installs a second kernel next to the
framework (and pnpm, which npm apps don't have); a package.json that
lists only @strutvane/framework was not detected as a project; `about`,
`help` sources and generated headers named the absorbed package.

- CLI_PACKAGE = '@strutvane/framework' (about, help, generated headers)
- project detection accepts @strutvane/framework (and still
  @strutvane/cli, so older apps are found and told what to remove)
- doctor `cli-local`: checks the framework, and the hint uses the
  project's own package manager (npm by default)
- doctor `absorbed` / `absorbed-transitive` (new, fail): any of
  @strutvane/{core,contracts,devkit,cli} or the `strutvane` launcher
  declared or installed next to the framework. Two kernels break
  container tokens and instanceof error checks, and @strutvane/cli and
  strutvane declare the same bins as the framework. The hint gives the
  remove command and the new import paths.
- Node.js >=24.3 (engines.node and doctor's `node` check; earlier 24.x
  break arguments in PowerShell, blueprint §5)
- dev-server hint says `npm install`, not `pnpm install`

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: vishwajitvm <vishwajitmall50@gmail.com>
